   "source": [
    "## 6. What this means for the forecast (S2-08)\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Weekdays drive the workload.** Mondays are the busiest day for every department; weekends are quiet. That's why the\n",
    "  method averages each weekday separately instead of using one daily average.\n",
    "- **Month-end is busier,** by the factor printed above (about 1.2). The method multiplies the 25th to month-end by it.\n",
    "- **No gaps:** every day of the year has a count, so the method never divides by a missing day.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Honest limits (say these to the panel):** the dates in this history were *assigned* to the past tickets in S1-06, with a\n",
    "realistic pattern (busier Mondays, month-end and winter), not recorded at Kopano Freight. The forecast shows how Relay's\n",
    "method works; its numbers aren't a prediction of the real company."
   ]
